<p>Decide before you start: am I learning, so I vibe-code, or am I shipping, so I direct an agent. Mixing the two is exactly how prototypes rot into fragile products. The discipline is a single sentence written before any tool opens. Applied: at the top of every build session you write "Mode: learning, output is disposable" or "Mode: shipping, output is owned and reviewed." That sentence is what stops the afternoon Bolt demo from becoming, by accident and inertia, the thing your customers run on next quarter.</p>

